course: dictionary
lesson: 13838
title: Jealously: two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jealously is an adverb. It tells you how someone does an action. It can mean feeling upset that someone else has something you want, or it can mean doing something very carefully to protect it. Check the clues around the word to find out which meaning is right.
explain: «Max watched jealously as his sister opened her new bike.» He is not just watching. The clue is that his sister has something he wants, so jealously means feeling upset and wanting what she has. Ask yourself: is someone wanting something, or someone guarding something?
explain: «The old king kept his gold jealously guarded in a locked room.» Here there is no wanting. The gold is locked away, so jealously means very carefully, to keep it safe. Try your meaning in the sentence: «kept his gold very carefully guarded» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Jealously means in a jealous way: feeling upset that someone has what you want.
fact: «Max watched jealously as his sister opened her new bike.» Max wanted the bike too.
fact: Jealously can also mean very carefully, protecting something: «a jealously guarded secret».
fact: In the Bible story of Joseph, his brothers were jealous of him, and it made them behave badly.
fact: Jealously is an adverb, so it often comes right after a verb, like «watched jealously» or «guarded jealously».
exercise: In «Max watched jealously as his sister opened her new bike», how is Max watching? | Sleepily, with his eyes closing | Calmly and happily | Very quietly, so nobody notices | *Feeling upset that his sister has something he wants
exercise: «The jewels were jealously guarded in a locked box.» What does jealously mean here? | *Very carefully, keeping them safe | Loudly, for everyone to hear | Angrily, with a shout | Without any care at all
exercise: In «Ella looked jealously at the girl's shiny red kite», what is Ella feeling? | *Wishing she had the kite herself | Bored and sleepy | Scared of the wind | Happy for the girl
test: «The old lady guarded her recipe jealously, and never shared it.» What does jealously mean here? | Happily, with a big smile | Quickly, in a hurry | *Very carefully, keeping it safe from others | Loudly, for all to hear
test: «Lily looked jealously at her friend's new puppy.» What feeling does jealously show? | Wanting to play hide and seek | *Wanting something that belongs to someone else | Feeling sorry for the puppy | Being very tired after a long walk
exam: «The girl guarded her diary jealously, so nobody could read it.» What does jealously mean here? | Happily, sharing it with everyone | Sadly, because she had lost it | Lazily, without thinking | *Very carefully, keeping it safe from others
